    "title": "Safe Workspace comes to hosted Harness deployments",
    "intro": "A focused nightly that extends Aura's Safe Workspace isolation model beyond desktop projects, so hosted-local Web projects running on a capable Harness can finally opt into per-session worktrees — with a clean fallback for older deployments.",
    "entries": [
      {
        "batch_id": "entry-1",
        "time_label": "3:34 AM",
        "started_at": "2026-07-29T10:34:47.000Z",
        "ended_at": "2026-07-29T10:34:47.000Z",
        "title": "Safe Workspace on hosted Harness with capability-gated fallback",
        "summary": "Safe Workspace isolation is now available for hosted-local Web projects, routed through the Harness lifecycle when it advertises support and hidden otherwise.",
        "items": [
          {
            "text": "Hosted-local Web projects can now execute chat turns inside an isolated Safe Workspace via a new hosted-Harness code path, alongside the existing desktop server-owned flow, by resolving an explicit execution-workspace authority (Aura server, hosted Harness, or Swarm) per request.",
            "commit_shas": [
              "28c45cb07ca2680509358a5a8c36053867480b21"
            ],
            "confidence": "high"
          },
          {
            "text": "Older hosted Harness deployments fail closed: the server checks a `safe_workspace: true` capability before accepting a safe turn, returns a clear 'not supported by the currently deployed hosted harness' error otherwise, and the AgentChatPanel hides the Safe Workspace control when the capability is absent.",
            "commit_shas": [
              "28c45cb07ca2680509358a5a8c36053867480b21"
            ],
            "confidence": "high"
          },
          {
            "text": "Remote/Swarm agents are explicitly rejected with a dedicated 'not yet available for remote agents' error, keeping the existing execution model intact for those sessions.",
            "commit_shas": [
              "28c45cb07ca2680509358a5a8c36053867480b21"
            ],
            "confidence": "high"
          },
          {
            "text": "Documented that foreground child agents inherit the parent's resolved project path, so a safe parent keeps its spawned children in the same session worktree without changes to spawn or streaming behavior.",
            "commit_shas": [
              "28c45cb07ca2680509358a5a8c36053867480b21"
            ],
            "confidence": "high"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
